13972	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s8","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s8-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:26:43.150Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac24, ac25 and ac26 of Story s8 in DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e are each designed: inbound recording at implement/validate/on request with the tracker user as author and framework posts skipped (ac24), first-line kind (ac25), once-only post with a receipt and no mirroring of edits/deletions (ac26), plus HLD binding requirement 4 (receipt keyed by feedback id, stable marker, listComments reconciliation before an uncertain retry).","evidence":"DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json:1756-1780 states ac24 ('recorded once as feedback with the tracker user as author, and the framework's own posts are never recorded'), ac25 (first-line revision/suggestion kind), ac26 ('posted once and marked as in the tracker, and a later edit or deletion on the tracker is not mirrored'). docs/plans/core-data-model.md:232 states requirement 4. LLD §2.1, §2.2, §3.2, §5 and §8.1 cover each: syncUnitComments called from implement/validate and tracker.syncComments; classifyComment; marker <!-- insrc:feedback:<artifactId>:<feedbackId> --> plus listComments reconciliation; a revision-less receipt keyed by feedbackId. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-2f27754d4ad00b8e.json, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Having isFrameworkComment recognise the unmarked pre-Story 'Attached <type> `<id>`: <link>' comment shape is within scope (§2.3, §7 Backward compat).","evidence":"docs/plans/core-data-model.md:222 (owner ruling 2, 'No compatibility code'): 'Nothing is left in the code only to cope with older data or older tools ... Things may break on the v2 branch; artifacts are handled manually where needed.' The LLD's own §7 says the shape test exists only because 'Attach comments posted before this Story have no marker'. That is a reader kept only for older data, which the ruling rules out. [files: docs/plans/core-data-model.md, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Remove the legacy-shape recogniser from isFrameworkComment. Hand the existing unmarked attach comments to the s9 conversion (or to manual handling) and record that hand-off in docs/plans/core-data-model.md. Alternatively, get an explicit owner exception to ruling 2 and record it there.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Feedback already has a source field that FeedbackService.add does not pass through; IssueOps.comment answers nothing; the GitHub adapter's attach posts an unmarked 'Attached …' comment and answers the comment id.","evidence":"artifact-core/types.ts:87 Feedback has `source?: { system; externalId; url? }`. history.ts:77-79 validateFeedback already validates a source. feedback-service.ts:28-37 FeedbackInput has no source; the entry built at :75-86 sets none, and the repeat check at :69-70 does not compare one. port.ts:63 `comment(issue, body): PortResult<void>`. github-adapter.ts:198-199 attach posts `Attached ${artifact.type} \\`${artifact.entityId}\\`: ${link}` through ghPostCommentReturningId and returns { externalId }. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/feedback/feedback-service.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A Story's binding lives on its LLD and a Task's binding lives on its TASK head, found with taskHeadIdOf; s6's attach reconciliation matches by link, so adding a marker line leaves it working.","evidence":"attach.ts:57-61 unitArtifactId gives lldArtifactId(epicHash, storyId) for a story unit. unit-issue.ts:79 gives taskHeadIdOf(...) for a task unit. lookup.ts:59 exports taskHeadIdOf. attach.ts:144 `known.find(c => c.text.includes(link))` reconciles by link, so a prepended marker line does not change the match. [files: src/workflow/tracker/attach.ts, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused pieces exist with the stated shapes: ghPostCommentReturningId posts and answers the comment id; listComments(issue, since?) returns TrackerComment {externalId, author, text, at, url?}; openTracker answers a port or a skip; readBinding(repoPath, artifactId) answers a binding or undefined. postComment does not already exist.","evidence":"github.ts:301-305 ghPostCommentReturningId(owner, repo, ref, body): string throws GhCommandError('rejected') when there is no numeric id. port.ts:72-79 defines TrackerComment and port.ts:98 listComments. tracker-auto.ts:175 openTracker returns { cfg, port } | { skip }. binding.ts:85 readBinding. A grep for postComment finds no definition in src/. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/tracker/binding.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The call-site inventories in §3 cover every file the change touches. §3.3 names the GitHub adapter and 'the test fake' as the TrackerPort implementations.","evidence":"Three TrackerPort implementations define listComments: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/approve-fallback-kit.ts and src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/attach.test.ts. Adding a required postComment breaks the typecheck of the attach.test.ts fake, which is not listed. §3 also never lists the callers that §2.6 and migration step 5 need: src/daemon/index.ts (where 'tracker.attach' is registered at :667, and where 'tracker.syncComments' must go), the new daemon handler file (cf. src/daemon/tracker-attach.ts), and src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts and validate.ts, where the sync is called. [files: src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/attach.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/approve-fallback-kit.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"Add these to the inventory: both TrackerPort fakes, src/daemon/index.ts, the new daemon handler module, and the implement and validate phase files.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"FeedbackInput.source is additive: no existing caller passes it and stored feedback is unchanged.","evidence":"feedback-service.ts:28-37 has no source today, so no caller can pass one. history.ts:77 already validates an optional source on stored lines, so older lines without one still validate. [files: src/workflow/feedback/feedback-service.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A revision-less receipt appended to the artifact's log has no effect beyond recording the post: it 'moves no revision and no status' (§4 sc4, §5 invariant).","evidence":"checkIntegrity (lifecycle.ts:131-140) compares the head only against the LAST log entry: `if (head.contentHash === '' || logTail?.revision === undefined) return { ok: true };`. History.logTail (history.ts:114-117) returns the last entry whatever its kind. lifecycle-service.ts:89 and :250 run this check on approve/complete. A receipt appended after the last content entry therefore turns the head-against-log check (log-ahead-of-head, hash-mismatch) into an automatic pass until the next content write. Every sync can append receipts to an LLD or TASK log. The s7 build-round entries (task-set.ts:368) already do this for TASK heads, but s8 extends it to Story LLDs and to every posted entry, and the LLD does not mention it. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"State this interaction. Either have checkIntegrity compare against the last log entry that carries a revision (an s3 change, per ruling 3's 'the log's last content entry': coordinate it or file it as an amendment), or keep receipts out of the log tail the check reads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The changes to code other Stories own are additive and raised for resolution, not silent redesigns: TrackerPort.postComment (s6/sc6), the attach comment text (s6), FeedbackInput.source (s5).","evidence":"Open questions 1-3 in §10 name each change and its owner and offer an alternative. HLD requirement 4 (core-data-model.md:232) assigns the port side to 's6 (port) and s8 (sync)', and s6 shipped no id-returning post on IssueOps (port.ts:63 still answers void), so adding a method here is within that joint ownership. The sc6 binding shape is left unchanged; alternative a2, which would change it, is rejected. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A failed inbound recording leaves the call repeatable: the since point is the latest tracker-sourced entry's time less a margin, so a comment that failed to record is read again on the next sync (§2.1 'can be repeated', §5 edge 'since point').","evidence":"FeedbackService.add stamps an entry with the local clock at recording time (feedback-service.ts:79 `timestamp: (this.deps.now ?? ...)().toISOString()`), not with the comment's creation time. Take comments A (older) and B (newer) read in one sync: if A's add fails transiently (an I/O error on the sidecar append) and B records, the next since point is B's recording time less a margin, which can be later than A's creation, so A is never listed again. A transient failure then becomes a permanent loss. Separately, GitHub's since filters on updated time (port.ts:97 'created or updated at or after it'). An old comment edited after recording is returned again, refused as 'already used with different content' (feedback-service.ts:71) and re-reported as failed on every sync after the edit; §5 does not state this. [files: src/workflow/feedback/feedback-service.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Derive the since point from data that survives a partial failure. Options: the earliest comment that failed this pass; the source's comment creation time stored on the entry and compared against the oldest unrecorded comment; or no since at all, using a full listComments with id-based repeats. State that a comment edited after recording is skipped silently, or reported once, rather than failing on every sync.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A comment author becomes the actor github:<login>, and only a login that cannot make a namespaced lower-case id falls back to github:unknown.","evidence":"decode.ts:47 isNamespacedActorId requires `id === id.toLowerCase()`, and FeedbackService.add refuses any other actor (feedback-service.ts:51-52). GitHub logins keep their case (for example 'Subho-Ghosh'). The LLD never says to lowercase the login. §5 sends any login that 'does not make a namespaced lower-case id' to github:unknown, so read literally, every mixed-case author is recorded as unknown. That breaks ac24's 'with the tracker user as author'. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts, src/workflow/feedback/feedback-service.ts]","action":"Specify that the login is lower-cased (GitHub logins are case-insensitive), giving github:<lowercased login>. Keep github:unknown only for empty or deleted authors, and cover a mixed-case login in the unit test 'the author ... derived from a tracker comment'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to at least one named test, at a level that exercises it.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping covers all three. ac24: comment-rules.test.ts (isFrameworkComment), comment-sync-inbound.test.ts and comment-sync-callers.test.ts (implement/validate/tracker.syncComments). ac25: comment-rules.test.ts classifyComment. ac26: comment-sync-outbound.test.ts (once-only, lost receipt found by marker, no mirroring), feedback-source.test.ts and port-post-comment.test.ts. The fixtures it names exist: src/workflow/__tests__/approve-fallback-kit.ts has a fake tracker with listComments. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/approve-fallback-kit.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":5,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-21T19:26:43.150Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
